<title>INDIA: BSE figures of India carry forward trade - Sept 21.</title>
<headline>BSE figures of India carry forward trade - Sept 21.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the latest data, for the top 10 stocks by value, released by the Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE) for the carry forward or &quot;badla&quot; account ended Sept 21</p>
<p>SCRIP		  SETTLEMENT  AV BADLA  QTY    VALUE    % BADLA</p>
<p>			 RATE				 (RS MLN)</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>State Bank	   265	   0.87     345750  91.62    17.12</p>
<p>Tata Steel	   175	   0.56     462800  80.99    16.69</p>
<p>Reliance	     197	   0.62     243300  47.93    16.41</p>
<p>L&amp;T		    240	   0.76     136600  32.78    16.51</p>
<p>ACC		   1860	   6.13	17040  31.69    17.18</p>
<p>Tata Power	   138	   0.45     167050  23.05    17.00</p>
<p>Tata Engg	    455	   1.53	41750  19.00    17.53</p>
<p>IPCL		   122	   0.40     137400  16.76    17.10</p>
<p>BSES Ltd	     183	   0.42	70300  12.86    11.97</p>
<p>Bajaj Auto	   989	   0.23	11400  11.27     1.21</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------- The average badla charges work out to 16.18 percent on an annualised basis against 14.47 percent in the previous carry forward account ended Sept 14.</p>
